    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p30-q16-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "He can row at 8 km/h and he can run at 10 km/h. He rows to a point on the shore $x$ km from $A$, and then he runs to $B$.\n\nShow that the time taken for the journey is $$T=\\frac{\\sqrt{36+x^2}}{8}+\\frac{20-x}{10}.$$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$T=\\dfrac{\\sqrt{36+x^2}}{8}+\\dfrac{20-x}{10}$ hours, for $0\\le x\\le20$.",
          "worked": "By Pythagoras, the distance rowed is $\\sqrt{6^2+x^2}=\\sqrt{36+x^2}$ km. The distance run is $20-x$ km.\n\nUsing $\\text{time}=\\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{speed}}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}T&=T_{\\text{row}}+T_{\\text{run}}\\\\T&=\\frac{\\sqrt{36+x^2}}{8}+\\frac{20-x}{10}.\\end{align*}$$\nHere $T$ is in hours and $0\\le x\\le20$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p30-q16-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Show that the time for the journey is minimised if he lands 8 km from $A$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The minimum occurs at $x=8$, so he should land 8 km from $A$.",
          "worked": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p30-q16-b-derivative",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
